\title{00 · Charter}
\taxon{Chapter}
\meta{origin}{design/00-charter.md}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{chapter}


\subtree{
  \title{Purpose}
  \p{A Lean 4 library of category theory whose only primitive is the virtual double ∞-category, built so that ordinary categories, ∞-categories, enriched and internal categories, and equipments are instances of one definition rather than parallel developments, and so that every theorem is proved once against an interface and never against an implementation.}
  \p{The library is built by agents against definitions frozen by a human. The definitions, their acceptance tests, and the interface are the product. Proofs are the cost of goods.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Non-goals}
  \ul{
    \li{Not a general-purpose mathematics library. Algebra, analysis, and topology are out of scope; "spaces" are Kan complexes and geometric realization is never needed.}
    \li{Not a contribution to Mathlib. Mathlib is scaffolding (→ \ref{dec-ch-0008}) and is hidden after the seal.}
    \li{Not constructive. Universal properties are propositions and witnesses are chosen classically (→ \ref{dec-ch-0002}).}
    \li{Not a home for defeq-based ergonomics. If a proof closes by \code{rfl} against an implementation, it is wrong for this library (→ \ref{dec-ch-0001}).}
    \li{Not a library of strict higher category theory. Strict ω-categories, computads, orientals, and rewriting exist in the kernel only, to build shape categories; nothing strict survives the seal.}
  }
}
